":75.7,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.0530609909839809,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":33.7,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.07490574481153989,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.1585740644685159,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.08723644424621835,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00773109243697479,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":87.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.0053399997,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.25,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":25.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"American International Group, Inc. provides insurance products for commercial, institutional, and individual customers in North America and internationally. It operates through three segments: North America Commercial, International Commercial, and Global Personal. The company offers commercial and industrial property insurance, including business interruption and package insurance that cover exposure to made and natural disasters; general liability, environmental, commercial automobile liability, workers' compensation, excess casualty, and crisis management insurance products; risk-sharing and other customized structured programs for large corporate and multinational customers; professional liability insurance; and marine, energy-related property insurance products, aviation, political risk, trade credit, and trade finance products. It also provides group personal accident and business travel products for employees, associations, and other organizations; voluntary and sponsor-paid personal accident and supplemental health products for individuals; and personal auto and homeowners in selected markets, comprehensive extended warranty, device protection insurance, home warranty and related services, and insurance for high net-worth individuals. In addition, the company offers mortgage and other loans receivable, such as commercial mortgages, life insurance policy loans, commercial loans, and other loans and notes receivable. American International Group, Inc. was founded in 1919 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jon  Hancock | EVP & Chief Executive Officer of General Insurance | Age 59 | Compensation: $5.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 22K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue falling 8%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["American International Group, I is a large-cap financial services business with a $43.0B market cap on $26.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -22% over the past three years and -7% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 10.8\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 15.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 33% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.33469784466289265},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $18.1M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-18088333.67},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 55% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"10,507 Shares of American International Group, Inc. $AIG Bought by Citizens & Northern Corp","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/10507-shares-of-american-international-group-inc-aig-bought-by-citizens-northern-corp.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794562151.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"American International Group (AIG) Could Be 7% Below Fair Value As Earnings And Dividend Hold","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-aig/american-international-group/news/american-international-group-aig-could-be-7-below-fair-value","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794547570.878,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.958,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Machina Capital S.A.S. Sells 19,760 Shares of American International Group, Inc. $AIG","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/machina-capital-s-a-s-sells-19760-shares-of-american-international-group-inc-aig.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794480354.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.863,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Learn Why The Bull Case For AIG Stock Could Change Following Earnings Beat","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-aig/american-international-group/news/learn-why-the-bull-case-for-aig-stock-could-change-following","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794458732.514,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why American International Group (AIG) is a Top Value Stock for the Long-Term","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028140/why-american-international-group-aig-is-a-top-value-stock-for-the